WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.003
A blog is a list of posts that visitors can browse by category

00:00:05.003 --> 00:00:08.241
and by tag, with a menu to find their way around.

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:11.479
In this video, you build one with The Blog Theme:

00:00:11.479 --> 00:00:14.540
a category, a post with tags, and a menu item.

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:22.049
The Blog recipe sets up a site for a blog.

00:00:22.049 --> 00:00:26.654
It creates the content types, a blog with a first post, the Categories

00:00:26.654 --> 00:00:31.260
and Tags taxonomies, and a Main Menu, and it activates The Blog Theme.

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:33.649
The Blog is a list.

00:00:33.649 --> 00:00:38.434
It contains Blog Posts, shown with the most recent first, and it is

00:00:38.434 --> 00:00:40.532
the home page of the site.

00:00:40.532 --> 00:00:44.990
Each post has a title, a subtitle, a banner image, and a body.

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:49.476
A taxonomy is a set of terms that you attach to content.

00:00:49.476 --> 00:00:54.297
A post can have one category, chosen from the Categories taxonomy, and any

00:00:54.297 --> 00:00:57.370
number of tags, taken from the Tags taxonomy.

00:00:57.370 --> 00:00:59.780
Both appear as badges on the post.

00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:04.492
You add a category, write a post, see where its tags are kept,

00:01:04.492 --> 00:01:06.764
and add an item to the Main Menu.

00:01:06.764 --> 00:01:09.327
Along the way, you meet the permalink:

00:01:09.327 --> 00:01:12.240
the address that each page gets on the site.

00:01:16.444 --> 00:01:19.959
This is the home page of the site, and it is the Blog.

00:01:19.959 --> 00:01:22.830
The banner shows its title and description.

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:27.049
Below come the posts, each with a subtitle, an author, a date, and

00:01:27.049 --> 00:01:29.334
badges for its category and tags.

00:01:29.797 --> 00:01:33.882
At the top right, the Main Menu holds two items, Home and About.

00:01:33.882 --> 00:01:36.567
The name of the site stands on the left.

00:01:37.026 --> 00:01:41.502
Opening a post shows its banner image, title, subtitle, and body.

00:01:41.502 --> 00:01:45.726
Under the text, the category and each tag link to a page that

00:01:45.726 --> 00:01:47.806
lists the posts they share.

00:01:48.259 --> 00:01:52.328
In the admin, the Blog item of the menu opens the Blog and

00:01:52.328 --> 00:01:54.108
the list of its posts.

00:01:54.108 --> 00:01:59.639
Create Blog Post adds a post to this blog, and Edit Blog changes the blog itself.

00:02:00.099 --> 00:02:02.807
Edit Blog shows how the blog is addressed.

00:02:02.807 --> 00:02:06.754
Its Permalink is blog, and a note says that this content item is

00:02:06.754 --> 00:02:10.589
the current homepage, which is why the site opens on the blog.

00:02:11.043 --> 00:02:14.448
The footer at the bottom of every page is a widget.

00:02:14.448 --> 00:02:18.091
In the admin, Design, Widgets opens Widgets and Layers:

00:02:18.091 --> 00:02:22.273
the Footer zone holds it, and its badge names the layer, Always.

00:02:26.477 --> 00:02:29.361
Categories are the terms of a taxonomy.

00:02:29.361 --> 00:02:34.232
In the admin menu, Content, Taxonomy lists the taxonomies of the site.

00:02:34.232 --> 00:02:36.027
Let's edit Categories.

00:02:36.490 --> 00:02:39.363
The editor lists the terms of the taxonomy:

00:02:39.363 --> 00:02:40.477
here, Travel.

00:02:40.477 --> 00:02:44.816
Add Category creates a category at the top level, and the Add button

00:02:44.816 --> 00:02:47.630
of a term creates a subcategory inside it.

00:02:48.086 --> 00:02:49.576
Let's add Photography.

00:02:49.576 --> 00:02:51.916
The title is the name of the category.

00:02:51.916 --> 00:02:56.436
The Permalink is the end of the address of its page, so let's type photography.

00:02:56.891 --> 00:02:58.899
The Icon field is required.

00:02:58.899 --> 00:03:02.853
It opens a picker, and the icon appears next to the name of

00:03:02.853 --> 00:03:04.740
the category on the site.

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:09.181
On this page, Publish adds the category to a draft of the taxonomy.

00:03:09.643 --> 00:03:15.149
A draft is not visible to visitors, so the taxonomy needs a Publish of its own.

00:03:15.149 --> 00:03:18.453
After that, the category is part of the site.

00:03:22.651 --> 00:03:26.346
From the Blog, Create Blog Post opens the editor of a post.

00:03:26.346 --> 00:03:29.586
Let's type the title and leave the Permalink empty:

00:03:29.586 --> 00:03:34.191
the address is built from the blog and the title, unless you type your own.

00:03:34.654 --> 00:03:39.778
The body is written in Markdown, which is plain text with simple marks for formatting.

00:03:39.778 --> 00:03:41.394
Let's write a sentence.

00:03:41.855 --> 00:03:44.371
The Subtitle shows under the title.

00:03:44.371 --> 00:03:48.177
For the Banner Image, Add media opens the media library:

00:03:48.177 --> 00:03:50.325
select an image and click OK.

00:03:51.654 --> 00:03:53.504
Tags searches as you type.

00:03:53.504 --> 00:03:56.801
Type to search the tags that exist, and select one.

00:03:56.801 --> 00:03:58.594
Let's select Exploration.

00:03:59.069 --> 00:04:03.479
When no tag matches, the field offers Press enter to create a tag.

00:04:03.479 --> 00:04:05.929
Let's type Lisbon and press Enter:

00:04:05.929 --> 00:04:10.399
the tag is created in the Tags taxonomy and selected for this post.

00:04:10.873 --> 00:04:15.470
Category lists the categories of the taxonomy, and a post can have one.

00:04:15.470 --> 00:04:18.933
Only a category without subcategories can be chosen.

00:04:18.933 --> 00:04:20.783
Let's choose Photography.

00:04:21.248 --> 00:04:25.158
Publish saves the post and returns to the Blog, with a message that

00:04:25.158 --> 00:04:26.658
the post is published.

00:04:26.658 --> 00:04:28.854
The list shows the post at the top.

00:04:28.854 --> 00:04:31.638
Save Draft would keep it hidden from visitors.

00:04:32.097 --> 00:04:36.096
On the site, the post comes first on the home page, with badges

00:04:36.096 --> 00:04:38.762
for Photography, Exploration and Lisbon.

00:04:38.762 --> 00:04:42.297
Opening it shows the banner, the subtitle and the text.

00:04:46.496 --> 00:04:48.699
Each tag links to a page of its own.

00:04:48.699 --> 00:04:52.686
Lisbon lists the posts that have this tag, which is the post we wrote.

00:04:53.145 --> 00:04:56.082
Tags are the terms of the Tags taxonomy.

00:04:56.082 --> 00:05:01.189
In the admin, Content, Taxonomy lists it, and its editor holds Lisbon next

00:05:01.189 --> 00:05:02.721
to the other tags.

00:05:02.721 --> 00:05:06.105
A tag created from a post is published at once.

00:05:06.568 --> 00:05:08.826
Add Tag creates a tag here as well.

00:05:08.826 --> 00:05:12.461
The tag field of a post creates tags only for users who have

00:05:12.461 --> 00:05:14.608
the Manage taxonomies permission.

00:05:18.815 --> 00:05:22.723
Main Menu in the admin menu opens the editor of the menu.

00:05:22.723 --> 00:05:25.080
Its Alias field holds main-menu:

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:29.545
The Blog Theme finds the menu by this alias, so keep it unchanged.

00:05:29.999 --> 00:05:34.123
Below, the editor lists the items, Home and About.

00:05:34.123 --> 00:05:38.689
Add Menu Item opens a dialog named Available Menu Items.

00:05:39.151 --> 00:05:40.937
It offers three types.

00:05:40.937 --> 00:05:45.339
A Link Menu Item links to a custom address, a Content Menu Item

00:05:45.339 --> 00:05:49.549
links to a content item, and an Html Menu Item uses HTML for

00:05:49.549 --> 00:05:51.271
the text of the link.

00:05:51.727 --> 00:05:53.732
Let's add a Link Menu Item.

00:05:53.732 --> 00:05:58.047
The Name is the text visitors see, and the Url is where it leads.

00:05:58.047 --> 00:06:01.207
Photography leads to the page of the category.

00:06:01.664 --> 00:06:05.748
Publish adds the item to a draft of the menu, and the editor

00:06:05.748 --> 00:06:07.976
lists it after Home and About.

00:06:07.976 --> 00:06:13.544
As with a taxonomy, visitors see the change only after the menu itself is published.

00:06:14.003 --> 00:06:15.590
Let's publish the menu.

00:06:15.590 --> 00:06:19.476
Dragging an item changes its order, and the Add button of an item

00:06:19.476 --> 00:06:23.143
adds an item inside it, which the theme shows as a drop-down.

00:06:23.615 --> 00:06:26.800
On the site, the menu shows Photography after About.

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:31.195
Clicking it opens the page of the category, which lists the post we wrote.

00:06:33.195 --> 00:06:35.015
A blog needs a few parts:

00:06:35.015 --> 00:06:39.302
a Blog with its posts, categories and tags to organize them, a Main

00:06:39.302 --> 00:06:42.708
Menu to move around, and a permalink for every page.

00:06:42.708 --> 00:06:44.235
Thanks for watching.

